1
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:17,500
Those who ceaselessly hone the art
of killing are known as masters.

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:22,197
These lethal abilities, dutifully
passed down through many generations,

3
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:25,177
have become what are
called modified bloodlines.

4
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:28,440
This is the story of one such master,

5
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:34,060
Hikaru Gero of the Poison Clan and his
greatest challenge yet, to get married.

6
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:57,177
No mama, lots of time.

7
00:01:23,486 --> 00:01:24,316
Toxic!

8
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,220
Kill or kiss

9
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:51,037
Let's go!

10
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:54,237
Kill a kiss, can't kill a kiss.

11
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:57,737
Kill a kiss, can't kill a kiss.

12
00:01:57,820 --> 00:02:01,600
Kill a kiss, can't kill a kiss.

13
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,417
Never forget Ghetto, the key
is to size up your target.

14
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:13,017
Observe the machine, the prize's position.

15
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:15,477
Note the strength of the
claw's grip and so on.

16
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,325
Then when the moment is right?

17
00:02:18,660 --> 00:02:19,660
You strike!

18
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,020
How complex.

19
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,200
Now you give it a try!

20
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:28,717
Crane games are evergreen
in the dating world.

21
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,957
The more effortless you
make it look, the better.

22
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:33,300
Earn a high score in the game of love.

23
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:34,440
Time to strike.

24
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:43,520
10,000 yen gone! Then again,

25
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:48,151
maybe you should steer clear of this
machine until you've had more practice.

26
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:49,657
Put it in a coin, hey?

27
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:51,200
That's more my speed.

28
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:54,900
Watch this.

29
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:01,720
Spotted garden eels!

30
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,150
Finish!

31
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:04,790
Perfect!

32
00:03:04,873 --> 00:03:06,780
You're number one! Congratulations!

33
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,620
I admit that was incredible.

34
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:12,575
But probably won't win you many girls.

35
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:14,900
Next game!

36
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:17,880
Let's go.

37
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:21,300
Why does this exist?

38
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:25,139
Let's make hunting memories
that'll last a lifetime.

39
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:32,980
By the way, Gero, speaking of
hunters... Now decorate! Did you hear?

40
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:38,177
You mean the hitman hunter that's
going around killing masters?

41
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:41,731
No one knows who or what they
want, but they're no amateur.

42
00:03:43,460 --> 00:03:47,401
Dan the Dismemberer and Kushima
the Spearmaster both got taken out.

43
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:50,197
Masters are the best assassins out there.

44
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:54,339
I doubt there are many people who
could take Kushima on head-to-head.

45
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:56,112
You'd better be careful.

46
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:57,430
Right.

47
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:00,140
Aw, it's so cute! All done!

48
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,967
Was this supposed to be fun?

49
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:05,200
No one likes a party pooper, Gedo.

50
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,769
Then I rescind my comment.

51
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:11,575
Remember, it's all about the memories.

52
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:15,042
We're commemorating the
fun both of us had today.

53
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,737
Is that how it works?

54
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:18,537
Would you like to print out this memory?

55
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:19,757
You'd be happy, right?

56
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:23,134
If a girl started talking
about DIY candy kits with you?

57
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:24,590
Well, yeah.

58
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,701
Don't try forcing a conversation.

59
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:31,417
But if you can get caught up
in something your date enjoys,

60
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:34,324
you might be surprised
by how much fun you have.

61
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:40,884
Guess we should call it a day -

62
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:51,640
Hikaru Gero, we need to talk.

63
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:57,360
But before we do, you have
to take a picture with me.

64
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:07,440
So, Kimi Arashiyama, let
me get this straight.

65
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:11,152
You want to hire Gero so you've
been following him around?

66
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:14,449
You could have reached
out on the dark nap.

67
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:18,555
There hasn't been a babe as
smokin' as me in centuries.

68
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:21,644
Frankly, you should be honored.

69
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:26,440
We call that a red flag. Wait!

70
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:29,837
You should hear me out before
you leave my life forever!

71
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:34,273
You know, stalking the guy you want
to hire doesn't exactly inspire trust.

72
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,320
You're right. I'm sorry.

73
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:42,300
For a sec, I was convinced the Hitman
Hunter had come to get Gato. Oh, yeah.

74
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:43,490
About that.

75
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:46,580
I'm actually a master, too.

76
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:49,180
Just like you.

77
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:52,717
Until someone comes along and
takes care of the hitman hunter.

78
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,859
I'm a target, too.

79
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:56,140
I'll let you protect me.

80
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,660
Come on, let's go.

81
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,780
You can't leave me!

82
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:01,637
You said you were a master, right?

83
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:03,617
So shouldn't you be able
to protect yourself?

84
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:06,760
I am, but you see, fighting
really isn't my thing.

85
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,571
I think we ought to stay and hear her out.

86
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:12,350
What?

87
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:13,610
Seriously?

88
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:18,517
If Arashiyama went through all this trouble
to seek help from a complete stranger,

89
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,659
she must be in a pretty tight spot.

90
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,130
Right?

91
00:06:25,213 --> 00:06:26,043
Arashiyama?

92
00:06:26,126 --> 00:06:27,860
Arashiyama? Arashiyama? Arashiyama?

93
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:31,290
Hey!

94
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,820
Hey, Master Hikaru, seriously
being this nice to me?

95
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:39,857
Look, her face!

96
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:43,705
Not only that, he's holding me
in his arms, calling out my name.

97
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:47,293
Actually paying attention to
me is still good to be true!

98
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:50,877
When I found out the hitman hunter
was after me, I was terrified.

99
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:53,577
Then as luck would have it,
I meet Master Hikaru Gator.

100
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:55,660
I didn't even make an appointment.

101
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:59,500
I bet it's inconvenient, but
he's treating me so courteously.

102
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:01,510
Arashiyama.

103
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,151
I think she's coming too.

104
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:10,809
Finally, I receive an
answer to my prayers!

105
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:18,257
Go ahead and give it your best shot,
sucker, because I'm untouchable!

106
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:20,693
Just try and take me out, Hitman Hunter!

107
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:24,511
Well, look, I never said I'd take the job.

108
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:27,140
Man, her lab sure does carry.

109
00:07:28,940 --> 00:07:29,800
Don't tell me.

110
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:33,320
You're wondering, just
what kind of master am I?

111
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:52,180
Let's start over.

112
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:55,280
My name's Kimi Arashiyama,
the Hamster Master.

113
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:57,480
This is my partner, Sirius.

114
00:07:58,380 --> 00:08:02,204
I'll have you know, he's the reason
I was able to track you down.

115
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:07,637
When it comes to intel gathering or
anything that requires a delicate touch,

116
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:10,014
me and my hamster are the ones to call.

117
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:11,759
Cuteness overload!

118
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:17,317
So you're related to the beast clan while

119
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:19,617
all masters might be
expertly trained killers?

120
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:22,177
They're not necessarily skilled in combat.

121
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:25,520
I'm more about assassination
and traps, for instance.

122
00:08:26,140 --> 00:08:28,857
You seriously consider that amateur hour?

123
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:30,197
For the record,

124
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:32,137
I didn't want anything
to do with The hitman

125
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:35,397
hunter but my association
said the hunt was on.

126
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:38,068
They're all fired up
about taking this jerk!

127
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:40,690
out.

128
00:08:40,773 --> 00:08:43,217
And you're in danger so you
want a bodyguard? Got it.

129
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:45,657
Instead of approaching
me why not ask someone

130
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:47,697
within your own clan to protect you from?

131
00:08:47,780 --> 00:08:48,610
They'd say no.

132
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:53,697
Up until my great-great-grandpa's
generation we were Ratmasters.

133
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:54,610
Even the

134
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:58,077
main Beast Clan respected us so
we had weight to throw around.

135
00:08:58,160 --> 00:09:01,877
But now our bloodline has thinned
out so much I wouldn't be surprised

136
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:05,548
if we ended up getting stripped
of our master title tomorrow.

137
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:10,135
I'm not exactly helping things
since I have zero kills.

138
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:12,617
This collar is the only link I have left.

139
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:15,641
All the branches of the
Beast Clan must wear them.

140
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:17,640
So you see how it is.

141
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:21,977
I show up to association
meetings when they tell me to,

142
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:25,797
but they've already decided the most
important stuff by the time I've arrived,

143
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:27,409
like taking on the hunter.

144
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,188
You know what they told me?

145
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:31,877
A master who doesn't or can't kill.

146
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:34,980
and works a normal job at a normal company

147
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:39,260
is only good for being
one thing, a shield.

148
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:43,392
Thank you for listening.

149
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:45,220
I've calmed down.

150
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:51,177
I got carried away earlier, like the future
head of one of the five great families?

151
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:53,577
would ever guard a branch family nobody.

152
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:56,660
Plus, there's no way I can
afford your massive fee.

153
00:09:57,760 --> 00:10:00,540
But I got to meet my fave before I died.

154
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:02,940
10,000 yen a day.

155
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:06,222
Just need to know when to start.

156
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:08,026
You're sure about this, Gero?

157
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:10,700
I mean...

158
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:12,674
You're in a real bind.

159
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:14,290
Aren't you?

160
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:18,420
All right.

161
00:10:18,660 --> 00:10:19,719
I guess it's fine.

162
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:21,817
This kind of derails my plans.

163
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:25,137
But at least Gero's charms are
starting to shine through on their own.

164
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:26,220
I'm proud of him.

165
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,122
I've dreamt of this for so long!

166
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,120
Advice! Help me!

167
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:37,180
Try hugging her back.

168
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:38,170
You're kidding!

169
00:10:38,253 --> 00:10:39,420
You know I can't!

170
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:45,000
Oh, there you are!

171
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:46,890
Hey!

172
00:10:46,973 --> 00:10:48,440
Okay, Hikaru Gero an assistant?

173
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:51,780
I'm taking you to meet the
rest of the association.

174
00:10:52,660 --> 00:10:55,248
Plus, they'll find out
about you eventually.

175
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:58,380
I guess this is the real Arashiyama.

176
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:04,620
She's the most unhinged woman so far,
but she is a fellow master. Who knows?

177
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:07,311
The two of them might actually hit it off.

178
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:10,800
We're here.

179
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,840
I'll handle introductions.

180
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:15,200
Serpent Master Ryuma.

181
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:17,320
Owl Master Chojabaru.

182
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:19,380
Hippo Master Shibaseki.

183
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:21,520
Orca Master Konkaiji.

184
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:23,720
Buffalo Master Heart.

185
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:25,840
Alligator Master Hamawaki.

186
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,077
Sleep on the job?

187
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:35,300
No, the animals are fine,
but the humans are dead.

188
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:45,877
Are you with the clan?

189
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:47,057
What happened?

190
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:49,000
He's not.

191
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:51,797
Hurry up!

192
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,060
Both of you, run!

193
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:05,697
So, uh, you're supposed to
be the poison master, right?

194
00:12:05,780 --> 00:12:08,397
I don't know what you're
doing here, but...

195
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:11,097
Hey, your timing's perfect!

196
00:12:11,180 --> 00:12:14,080
This saves me from
having to track you down.

197
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:16,797
You're a big name now!

198
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,527
I can cross you off my list.

199
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:24,650
Wait!

200
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:26,300
Did he just?

201
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:28,920
Stab Ghetto?

202
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:30,010
Run

203
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:31,197
Don't stand there!

204
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:32,500
Go, now!

205
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:39,177
Any deeper and it could have been fatal.

206
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:40,657
I've stopped the bleeding.

207
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:42,440
But it won't last.

208
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:44,977
So you're the hitman hunter?

209
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:46,820
What are you after?

210
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:03,320
He did that?

211
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:05,020
With one little knife?

212
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,280
This guy's not human!

213
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:23,709
I can't let this drag out.

214
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:25,777
Is there enough time to set a trap?

215
00:13:25,860 --> 00:13:26,760
Not a chance.

216
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:31,265
I've just got to face him head
on and go all out from the start.

217
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:35,400
Optical reflex accelerator.

218
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:37,140
Toxin vision.

219
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:39,540
Muscle reflex enhancer.

220
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:41,600
Toxin javelin strike.

221
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:47,228
That double dose should
end this fight fast.

222
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,820
What's up? Huh?

223
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:16,340
A mistake.

224
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:22,660
I hear you, but the Poison Master
is still an assassin, right?

225
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:26,329
He's taking bodyguard
gigs on the Dark Nav?

226
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:28,900
You sure you've got the right guy?

227
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:32,657
No one in the five families
would be caught dead doing that.

228
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:35,000
The thing is, he seems dangerous.

229
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:39,400
He shot two syringes into
his own neck. Two! I know.

230
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:42,540
Seems kind of risky, letting him go.

231
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:46,257
I feel it's probably for
the best if I take him out.

232
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:47,200
Yeah.

233
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:51,740
I'll beat him to the punch.

234
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:19,740
No way.

235
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,647
Toxic Vision's not able
to keep track of him?

236
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:24,860
That was a close one.

237
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:28,880
You guys okay?

238
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:36,660
Got a soft spot for animals, huh?

239
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:40,606
I mean, it's not like
they did anything wrong.

240
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:42,332
Where did you come from?

241
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:44,289
A branch of the Iron Clan?

242
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:47,840
I'm pretty sure I'm just a normal guy.

243
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:49,550
Impossible.

244
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:50,974
Which family sent you?

245
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:54,239
Man, why would I lie to
somebody who's about to die?

246
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:58,200
All of my relatives are teachers.

247
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:04,740
In that case, he's got to be a mutant.

248
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:08,797
Masters spend generations
building up their bloodlines,

249
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:11,537
but somehow this freak has
surpassed them in only one.

250
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:14,537
For lunch pretty soon
damn it I've never tried

251
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:20,220
this before but I've got
no choice toxin triple dose

252
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:26,260
Yikes come on why did you
go and do that it's suicide

253
00:16:29,820 --> 00:16:33,180
I should have known a triple
dose might have worked

254
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:37,000
if I hadn't already lost so much blood.

255
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:39,360
What did I tell you?

256
00:16:40,020 --> 00:16:41,700
You killed so many people.

257
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:45,696
After all the hatred you
spread, this is what you get.

258
00:16:48,580 --> 00:16:49,660
Time to die.

259
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:54,820
Just promise me one thing.

260
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:58,264
You won't touch either of them.

261
00:16:58,660 --> 00:16:59,520
Swear it.

262
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:10,660
Yo, Hitman Hunter!

263
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:14,540
Gator's not dying on my watch!

264
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:16,300
The rules just did a 180!

265
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:19,937
Uh, if you get in the way, I've
got to take care of you, too.

266
00:17:20,020 --> 00:17:21,440
Big dummy, shove it!

267
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:25,357
You think he's going
around spreading hatred?

268
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,600
Like hell he is!

269
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:30,520
He offered to be my bodyguard,
even when I couldn't pay him!

270
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:34,677
I wasn't gonna go down at
the shield for some jerk!

271
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:37,720
But I'm more than happy
to die for my idol!

272
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:41,420
Serious squad?

273
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:52,310
Ready?

274
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:59,637
Modify bloodline plus plus Feel the
wrath of Pontus Major unleashed?

275
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:03,880
The greater dog that
shines in the winter sky!

276
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:06,740
How do you like that, punk?

277
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,697
Where do you think you're taking him?

278
00:18:15,780 --> 00:18:16,610
Let go.

279
00:18:16,693 --> 00:18:17,660
What do you mean?

280
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:21,442
Obviously the hospital,
since he's dying and all.

281
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:24,100
You mean Canis Major actually worked?

282
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:26,700
You were dead set on killing me.

283
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:28,460
Why save my life?

284
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:31,230
Mmm.

285
00:18:31,313 --> 00:18:32,840
I've never seen that before.

286
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:35,337
Masters looking out for each other.

287
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:38,040
Plus, I don't feel like
killing you anymore.

288
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:39,575
Those are my reasons.

289
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:40,876
Good enough for you?

290
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:45,237
I see.

291
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:46,380
Put me down.

292
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:47,937
But your wounds...

293
00:18:48,020 --> 00:18:50,196
...are something I can handle myself.

294
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:53,500
My name's Pichi Nakagawa.

295
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:56,927
When's it my turn to
have his head on my lap?

296
00:18:58,280 --> 00:18:59,397
I have one goal.

297
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:03,480
Eliminating the Beast Clan, one of
the five great families for good.

298
00:19:03,620 --> 00:19:05,777
Rumor is they're planning something major,

299
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:08,477
something dangerous that'll
kill a whole lot of people.

300
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:12,207
I figured I'd take them out
before the damage got out of hand.

301
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:15,937
Then how come you're hunting
people outside of their clan?

302
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:17,720
I might as well. Come again?

303
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:21,737
See, I had no idea where
to even start looking,

304
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:25,297
so I asked anyone who could
steer me in the right direction.

305
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:29,617
Which led me to a homicidal
maniac they once did a deal with.

306
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:31,737
Then there was the guy
with the pointy stick.

307
00:19:31,820 --> 00:19:34,197
Plus those six from the branch families.

308
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:37,927
They weren't much help, but it's
not like I could let them go.

309
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:40,720
Wait, what maniac?

310
00:19:41,460 --> 00:19:44,220
Dan the Dismemberer He
didn't work for money.

311
00:19:44,820 --> 00:19:46,980
He took apart old men as payment.

312
00:19:48,280 --> 00:19:51,017
And Kushima the Spearmaster
He had a reputation

313
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:53,806
for involving innocent
bystanders in his jobs?

314
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:58,780
All I want is to open a
cafe with my girlfriend.

315
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:05,280
But before I can do that, somebody
needs to clean up the world.

316
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:07,920
Our poor customers.

317
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:10,200
How could they relax?

318
00:20:11,820 --> 00:20:13,880
Why is his head still on her lap?

319
00:20:14,340 --> 00:20:16,577
Feuding with one of the
five great families?

320
00:20:16,660 --> 00:20:18,460
Are you nuts? What?

321
00:20:18,740 --> 00:20:22,740
No, but wouldn't it be better without
these bad guys to worry about?

322
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:25,771
Normally, I'd write that off as a fantasy.

323
00:20:26,740 --> 00:20:30,034
But with his abilities, he
might be able to pull it off.

324
00:20:30,540 --> 00:20:32,340
Out of nowhere, there's you.

325
00:20:32,620 --> 00:20:35,237
I heard the family of
Poison Masters was bad.

326
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:37,320
But it turns out you're different.

327
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:40,602
Obviously, you're not dangerous.

328
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:42,721
At least not to the world I want.

329
00:20:43,580 --> 00:20:44,620
Not right now.

330
00:20:44,900 --> 00:20:46,371
But maybe that'll change.

331
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:51,380
So, uh, that means you're gonna
let us go, right? Come on!

332
00:20:52,060 --> 00:20:53,648
Well, problem solved, then!

333
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,270
Mr.

334
00:20:57,353 --> 00:20:59,337
Gato, you're from one
of the five families.

335
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:01,817
Maybe you can tell me what
the Beast Clan is up to.

336
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:03,488
Not like I'd know anything.

337
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:07,137
People call us the five great
families out of convenience.

338
00:21:07,220 --> 00:21:09,817
It's not like we have
any sort of connection.

339
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:10,900
That's too bad.

340
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:13,500
And what about you?

341
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:15,720
You're a branch of the Beast Clan.

342
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:16,770
Any leads?

343
00:21:17,220 --> 00:21:19,997
I've never been to the main
house or met the family.

344
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:20,910
That figures.

345
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:25,204
All I know is I have the collar
they give all the branch members.

346
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,310
Arashiyama!

347
00:21:31,020 --> 00:21:32,020
A bat?

348
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:35,317
What's wrong with her, Kato?

349
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,380
I don't know.

350
00:21:36,620 --> 00:21:38,385
I'm guessing it's this collar.

351
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:39,870
Easy.

352
00:21:39,953 --> 00:21:43,659
I wouldn't remove that unless you
wanted to completely drain a toast.

353
00:21:43,900 --> 00:21:47,917
The Bonda Constrictor is a living
accessory engineered to suck blood.

354
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:52,980
I went ahead and activated it, meaning
that woman's got three days to live, tops.

355
00:21:54,060 --> 00:21:55,037
Why make her aware?

356
00:21:55,120 --> 00:21:57,257
Wouldn't want him running off, would we?

357
00:21:57,340 --> 00:21:59,280
The livestock, that is.

358
00:22:01,040 --> 00:22:02,820
Spare me the death glare!

359
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:08,180
If you're actually interested in facing
me, Hikaru Gero and Piichi Nakagawa,

360
00:22:08,380 --> 00:22:09,733
here's your invitation.

361
00:22:09,900 --> 00:22:14,620
See me on the Beast Clan's
home turf, Dogo Animal Kingdom!

362
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:23,057
I'll be crazy.

363
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:24,797
Oh, make that noise.

364
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:25,957
Oh, I'll be crazy.

365
00:22:26,040 --> 00:22:27,440
Oh, make that noise.

366
00:22:28,660 --> 00:22:33,484
Ah, the
out-to-na-ni-yo-i-wata-si-bick-ri-dottk-ri-fum-da-ri-ke-t-ri-muh-ga-muchu.

367
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:38,460
Ah,
out-to-na-ni-yo-i-an-ata-hattari-ba-kari-un-zari-gakari-bye-bye-chu.

368
00:22:38,700 --> 00:22:43,449
I can't see it.

369
00:22:43,532 --> 00:22:44,362
I can't see it. I can't see it.

370
00:22:50,060 --> 00:22:52,777
Thank you

371
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:59,860
so

372
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:12,190
much

373
00:23:12,273 --> 00:23:13,520
for joining us.

374
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:49,320
This is 100 % a trap, for sure!

375
00:23:49,520 --> 00:23:51,837
This is what somebody who's
as good as mine can do!

376
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:53,155
Absolutely delicious.

377
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:55,260
Next time, the Animal Kingdom.
